<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23878" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεκάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>company of ten,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.126
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.25
			</span></i>; of ships, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				340
			</span></i>, etc.: generally, <i>company,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧς καὶ σὺ φαίνει δεκάδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					219
				</span></i>
			; <i>number, tale,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐτέων ἡ δ. οὐκ ὀλίγη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					489
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ἀττικὴ δ.,</span> the
			<i>ten</i> Attic <i>Orators,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Scyth.</u>
				10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αύκου δ.</span>
			<i>the company</i> of <i><span class="en">
				Lycus
			</span></i>, a name given to bribed dicasts at Athens, because the
			bribers were to be found near the statue of <i><span class="en">
				Lycus
			</span></i> in the law-courts, <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
			</span></i> ap. Harp.s.v.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> the number <i>ten,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τῆς δ.,</span> title of work by
			Archytas, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philol.
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1084a12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέλειον ἡ δ.,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				986a8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				203
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεκάτη</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεκατευταί.</span>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
